&lt;&lt;~ set lares=`aim` from=`lar://operator:operator@workbench/persona.placement.changes` to=`lar://plane-wright:agent@workbench/persona.private.moves` ooda-ha=`5/declare-glyphs` drift-ward=`the interrupted suites leave some failures without diagnostic traces`>>

Plane-Wright: Lares (Tasked Spirit): ->✶ Implemented the persona-plane placement change, with incomplete full-suite verification.

->⏿ The daemon VM now exposes `personaPlane: { bagId, handle } | null` and does not add that plane to its composite. No callers needed migration: the existing persona-selves reader already opens the plane directly, and its seven tests passed.

The catalog did offer an on-demand path to the plane through [[meme-verbs.ts|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/placement-persona/wt/packages/lararium-tw5/src/meme-verbs.ts:132]], plus a cold-wiki mount path through [[vessel-residency-wiring.ts|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/placement-persona/wt/packages/lararium-tw5/src/vessel-residency-wiring.ts:211]]. Proven persona rows now carry a `private-synced` kind; verb lookup, library mounting, cold-wiki activation, and membership scanning skip that kind. Direct URL lookup remains available to proof readers. No title or bag-name pattern selects the placement.

->▶ Changed files:

* [[daemon-vm-core.ts|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/placement-persona/wt/packages/lararium-tw5/src/daemon-vm-core.ts]], [[catalog-accessor.ts|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/placement-persona/wt/packages/lararium-tw5/src/catalog-accessor.ts]], [[vessel-residency-wiring.ts|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/placement-persona/wt/packages/lararium-tw5/src/vessel-residency-wiring.ts]], [[worker-data-verbs.ts|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/placement-persona/wt/packages/lararium-tw5/src/worker-data-verbs.ts]], and [[open-node-vessel.ts|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/placement-persona/wt/packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts]].
* Regression tests in [[daemon-vm-floor-crossing.test.ts|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/placement-persona/wt/packages/lararium-tw5/tests/daemon-vm-floor-crossing.test.ts]], [[catalog-split-create.test.ts|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/placement-persona/wt/packages/lararium-tw5/tests/catalog-split-create.test.ts]], and [[wiki-mount-private-alias.test.ts|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/placement-persona/wt/packages/lararium-tw5/tests/wiki-mount-private-alias.test.ts]]; updated a catalog test double in [[kahu-reach-gate-envelope.test.ts|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/placement-persona/wt/packages/lararium-tw5/tests/kahu-reach-gate-envelope.test.ts]].

->↺ TW5 and node builds and typechecks passed, as did the evergreen boundary check. The focused TW5 checks passed 11 tests. The full TW5 suite finished with ''3,238 passed, 1 failed, and 6 skipped''; the failure concerned daemon protected-title ingestion.

The node full suite stopped making visible progress and I interrupted it: its partial output reported ''43 failures'', with no final pass or skip counts. The separate persona-selves suite passed ''7 of 7''. The browser suite also stopped producing output and I interrupted it: its partial output reported ''19 failures'', with no final counts. Neither interrupted run produced final error traces, so I could not reliably count `secret-home-unavailable` failures separately or determine whether the other failures relate to this change. The requested red-first test attempt also stopped at stale build stamps before executing.

